    <DataNode elementId="AT4G15340-MONOMER" textLabel="arabidiol synthase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9FR95" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Arabidiol synthase is a member of the oxidosqualene cyclase (OSC) family of enzymes. Although it was originally named PEN1 based on sequence similarity to pentacyclic triterpene synthases |CITS: [11247608]|, this enzyme catalyzes the formation of a tricyclic terpene |CITS:[16774269][17474751]| when it is over-expressed in yeast or tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt;. This enzyme is the first reported example of a triterpene synthase that forms a single product with a water molecule as the source of a hydroxyl group |CITS:[16774269]|. Arabidiol synthase also produces some minor products &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and in yeast, including 14-epithalianol, an epimer of |FRAME:CPD-10263| |CITS:[17474751]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G15340-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G15340.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9FR95" />
